      "label": "Pricing Strategy",
      "group": "finance",
      "is_hub": false,
      "excerpt": "# Pricing Strategy\n\nOur pricing strategy at Bloom & Brew balances premium positioning with neighborhood accessibility. We're not the cheapest, but we deliver exceptional value.\n\n## Pricing Philosophy\n\n- Price reflects quality and experience, not just product cost\n- Maintain minimum 65% gross margin on coffee, 55% on floral\n- Round to psychologically appealing price points ($4.75 not $4.73)\n- Bundle pricing to increase average ticket size\n\n## Coffee Pricing\n\n| Item | Price | Margin |\n|------|-------|--------|\n| Drip coffee (12oz) | $3.50 | 78% |\n| Latte (12oz) | $5.25 | 68% |\n| Specialty drink | $6.50-7.50 | 62% |\n| Retail beans (12oz bag) | $16.00 | 55% |\n\n## Floral Pricing\n\n| Product | Price Range | Margin |\n|---------|------------|--------|\n| Small arrangement | $35-55 | 58% |\n| Medium arrangement | $65-95 | 55% |\n| Large/event | $120-250+ | 52% |\n| Workshop fee | $65-95/person | 72% |\n| Weekly subscription | $45/week | 50% |\n\n## Competitive Analysis\n\nWe survey competitor pricing quarterly. In our area, we're positioned 10-15% above chain coffee shops and comparable to other specialty caf\u00e9s. Our floral pricing is competitive with local florists but our workshop pricing is premium justified by the experience.\n\n## Discounts & Promotions\n\n- [[Loyalty Program]]: Every 10th coffee free (~10% effective discount)\n- [[Seasonal Campaigns]] may include limited-time pricing\n- [[Partnership Opportunities]] volume discounts capped at 15%\n- Staff discount: 50% off (tracked in [[Team Roster]])\n\n## Reviews\n\nPricing is reviewed in every [[Quarterly Business Review]] against [[Revenue Streams]] data and [[Budget Planning]] COGS trends. [[Inventory Management]] cost data feeds directly into margin calculations.\n"
