      "group": "finance",
      "is_hub": false,
      "excerpt": "# Revenue Streams\n\nBloom & Brew operates multiple revenue streams across our coffee and floral business lines. Diversification is key to weathering seasonal fluctuations.\n\n## Revenue Breakdown (Annual)\n\n| Stream | % of Revenue | Trend |\n|--------|-------------|-------|\n| Coffee (in-store) | 35% | Steady |\n| Floral arrangements | 25% | Growing |\n| Workshops & events | 15% | Growing fast |\n| Coffee subscriptions | 10% | Growing |\n| Retail (beans, merchandise) | 8% | Steady |\n| Corporate/wholesale | 7% | New, growing |\n\n## Coffee Revenue\n\nOur espresso bar is the daily traffic driver. Average ticket is $6.80, with 180-220 transactions per day. See [[Product Catalog]] for our full menu. [[Pricing Strategy]] covers our margin targets.\n\n## Floral Revenue\n\nCustom arrangements range from $35 (small) to $250+ (event pieces). Wedding season and holidays drive significant spikes \u2014 see [[Seasonal Campaigns]] for details. Our [[Partnership Opportunities]] with wedding planners generate high-value orders.\n\n## Workshops\n\nOur floral arrangement workshops ($65-$95/person, 8-12 participants) have become a surprise hit. They drive [[Email Marketing]] signups, [[Social Media Strategy]] content, and [[Loyalty Program]] engagement. Quarterly workshop revenue targets are tracked in [[Budget Planning]].\n\n## Subscriptions\n\nWeekly flower subscriptions ($45/week) and coffee subscriptions ($25/bi-weekly) provide predictable recurring revenue. We have 85 active flower subscribers and 140 coffee subscribers.\n\n## Growth Opportunities\n\nThe [[Growth Roadmap]] outlines our plan to grow corporate/wholesale to 15% of revenue through the [[Partnership Opportunities]] pipeline. The [[Quarterly Business Review]] tracks progress against targets.\n"
