      "excerpt": "# Partnership Opportunities\n\nStrategic partnerships extend Bloom & Brew's reach and create new [[Revenue Streams]] without significant capital investment.\n\n## Active Partnerships\n\n### The Magnolia Inn (Boutique Hotel, 2 blocks away)\n- We supply daily lobby arrangements and in-room welcome bouquets\n- Their guests receive 10% discount at our studio\n- Joint promotion in their guest welcome packet\n- Revenue: ~$1,200/month\n\n### Oakwood Community Center\n- Monthly floral arrangement workshop series\n- They provide the space, we provide materials and instruction\n- Split ticket revenue 70/30 (us/them)\n- Great for [[Email Marketing]] list growth\n\n### Local Wedding Planners Network\n- Preferred vendor status with 4 local wedding planners\n- Commission: 8% referral fee on bookings over $500\n- [[Product Catalog]] includes dedicated wedding packages\n\n## Partnership Pipeline\n\n| Partner | Type | Status | Expected Revenue |\n|---------|------|--------|-----------------|\n| Downtown Yoga Studio | Cross-promo | In talks | $400/mo |\n| Regional Hospital Gift Shop | Wholesale | Proposal sent | $2,000/mo |\n| Corporate Office Park | Subscription | Meeting scheduled | $3,500/mo |\n\n## Co-Branding Rules\n\nAll partnerships must adhere to our [[Brand Guidelines]]. Co-branded materials require approval from our marketing lead. Partner stories are featured in our [[Social Media Strategy]] content calendar.\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nWe evaluate partnerships quarterly in the [[Quarterly Business Review]] using: revenue generated, brand alignment, customer acquisition cost, and operational burden. [[Budget Planning]] tracks partnership-related expenses separately.\n"
