      "id": 23,
      "label": "Daily Standup Process",
      "group": "operations",
      "is_hub": false,
      "excerpt": "# Daily Standup Process\n\nOur daily standup meetings are the heartbeat of Bloom & Brew, our artisan coffee and floral design studio. Every morning at 8:45 AM, before the shop opens, the entire [[Team Roster]] gathers near the espresso bar for a quick 10-minute check-in.\n\n## Format\n\nEach team member answers three questions:\n1. What did you accomplish yesterday?\n2. What are you working on today?\n3. Any blockers?\n\n## Key Rules\n\n- Keep it under 10 minutes \u2014 if a topic needs deeper discussion, schedule a separate huddle\n- Stand up! No sitting allowed \u2014 it keeps energy high\n- The [[Shift Scheduling]] board should be updated before standup\n- Any issues with [[Inventory Management]] should be flagged here\n\n## Notes\n\nWe started this practice after our Q2 review showed communication gaps between the floral and coffee sides of the business. Since implementing standups, our [[Customer Feedback Program]] scores have improved by 18%. The [[Quarterly Business Review]] now tracks standup attendance as a KPI.\n\nSarah from the floral team suggested adding a \"kudos\" moment at the end where someone can shout out a teammate. This has been great for morale and ties into our [[Employee Wellness Program]].\n"
