      "label": "Inventory Management",
      "group": "operations",
      "is_hub": false,
      "excerpt": "# Inventory Management\n\nEffective inventory management is critical for Bloom & Brew since we deal with two highly perishable product categories: fresh flowers and specialty coffee beans.\n\n## Coffee Inventory\n\n- Green beans are ordered bi-weekly from our [[Supplier Relationships]] partners\n- Roasted beans have a 14-day freshness window\n- We maintain a minimum stock of 20 lbs per variety\n- Reorder triggers are managed through our spreadsheet system (see [[Tech Stack and Tools]])\n\n## Floral Inventory\n\n- Fresh flowers are sourced three times a week from local growers and the wholesale market\n- Seasonal availability drives our [[Product Catalog]] offerings\n- Waste tracking is essential \u2014 we aim for under 8% spoilage\n- Dried flower supplies for our workshop series are ordered monthly\n\n## Storage\n\nThe back room is split into zones: cold storage (flowers, 34-38\u00b0F), cool storage (beans, 60-65\u00b0F), and dry storage (packaging, retail items). The [[Facilities Maintenance]] schedule includes daily temperature checks.\n\n## Counting\n\nFull inventory counts happen every Sunday evening after close. The [[Shift Scheduling]] always assigns two people for this task. Discrepancies over $50 are reported in the [[Quarterly Business Review]].\n\n## Integration with Sales\n\nOur [[Revenue Streams]] analysis shows that inventory turns directly impact margin. The [[Pricing Strategy]] document outlines our markup targets per category.\n"
