      "excerpt": "# Supplier Relationships\n\nStrong supplier relationships are a competitive advantage for Bloom & Brew. We prioritize local, sustainable, and ethical sourcing across both our coffee and floral lines.\n\n## Coffee Suppliers\n\n### Altitude Roasters Cooperative (Primary)\n- Single-origin beans from Colombia, Ethiopia, and Guatemala\n- Fair trade certified, direct trade relationships\n- Delivery: Every other Monday\n- Payment terms: Net 30\n- Contact: Miguel Santos, miguel@altitudecoop.com\n\n### Local Dairy \u2014 Meadowbrook Farms\n- Whole milk, oat milk, cream\n- Delivery: Mon/Wed/Fri before 6 AM\n- Ties into our [[Brand Guidelines]] commitment to local sourcing\n\n## Floral Suppliers\n\n### Valley Bloom Wholesale\n- Primary source for roses, lilies, seasonal stems\n- Tuesday/Thursday/Saturday deliveries\n- We get first pick before 5 AM \u2014 early [[Shift Scheduling]] matters here\n\n### Dried & Preserved \u2014 Everlast Botanicals\n- Dried flowers, preserved eucalyptus, craft supplies for workshops\n- Monthly bulk orders, 15% volume discount above $500\n\n## Relationship Management\n\n- Quarterly check-ins with all primary suppliers\n- Annual review of terms during [[Quarterly Business Review]]\n- We feature supplier stories in our [[Social Media Strategy]] content\n- New supplier evaluation criteria are documented in the [[Pricing Strategy]] to ensure margin targets\n\n## Backup Suppliers\n\nWe maintain backup relationships for every critical category. Supply chain disruptions during previous years taught us this lesson. Details in [[Inventory Management]].\n"
